%N A398587 Decimal expansion of Re(Li_4(1 + i)), where Li_4(z) is the polylogarithm function of order 4, and i is the imaginary unit.
%H A398587 Seán Mark Stewart, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2478/tmmp-2020-0034">Explicit Evaluation of Some Quadratic Euler-Type Sums Containing Double-Index Harmonic Numbers</a>, Tatra Mountains Mathematical Publications, Vol. 77, No. 1 (2020), pp. 73-98; <a href="https://sciendo.com/pdf/10.2478/tmmp-2020-0034">alternative link</a>. See p. 95, eq. (46).
%H A398587 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.53, pp. 450-451, eq. (4.176) and (4.178), section 5.53, p. 468, section 6.53, pp. 770-779.
%H A398587 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polylogarithm">Polylogarithm</a>.
%H A398587 Ming Hao Zhao, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.12155">On logarithmic integrals, harmonic sums and variations</a>, arXiv:1911.12155 [math.CA], 2019-2020. See Proposition 9, p. 36.
%F A398587 Equals Re(Li_4(1 - i)).
%F A398587 Equals 485*zeta(4)/512 + log(2)^2*zeta(2)/8 - 5*log(2)^4/384 - 5*Li_4(1/2)/16.
%e A398587 0.959318913578419257202911220606297198707898070029425...
%t A398587 RealDigits[Re[PolyLog[4, 1+I]], 10, 120][[1]]
%t A398587 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398587 RealDigits[485*Zeta[4]/512 + Log[2]^2*Zeta[2]/8 - 5*Log[2]^4/384 - 5*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/16, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398587 (PARI) real(polylog(4, 1+I))
%o A398587 (PARI) 485*zeta(4)/512 + log(2)^2*zeta(2)/8 - 5*log(2)^4/384 - 5*polylog(4, 1/2)/16
%Y A398587 Cf. A002162, A013661, A013662, A099218, A398588.
%Y A398587 Re(Li_k(1 + i)): A222068 (k=2), A398585 (k=3), this constant (k=4).
